  "summary": "Aranmula Kannadi (Malayalam: ആറന്മുളക്കണ്ണാടി), meaning the Aranmula mirror, is a handmade, metal-alloy, first surface mirror made in Aranmula, a small town in Pathanamthitta in the state of Kerala, India.",
  "description": "Aranmula Kannadi (Malayalam: ആറന്മുളക്കണ്ണാടി), meaning the Aranmula mirror, is a handmade, metal-alloy, first surface mirror made in Aranmula, a small town in Pathanamthitta in the state of Kerala, India. The mirrors received a geographical indication (GI) tag in 2005.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Kerala; registration 2004–05), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
